{"results":[{"record_id":"june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000246","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper presents a multimodal LLM trained on 5.5M instruction-following examples across 70+ task types, including free-text biological QA and open-ended reasoning. This is broad, transferable pretraining rather than a narrow application wrapper.","evidence_snippet":"\"We introduce OmicsLM, a multimodal LLM\"; \"train OmicsLM on more than 5.5 million instruction-following examples spanning over 70 task types\"; \"open-ended biological question answering\"; \"language-guided, multi-sample reasoning\"; \"free-text biological knowledge\"; \"natural-language biological tasks\"; \"perform comparably to specialized omics models\"; \"outperforming ... general LLMs\"; \"continuous vector ... projecting it into the LLM token-embedding space\"; \"multiple profiles can be interleaved in one prompt\"; \"can use expression profiles directly and perform comparably to specialized omics models\"; \"language-guided biological reasoning over expression data\""},{"record_id":"june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000246","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model is explicitly an LLM with a generative language interface over omics inputs, so the candidate architecture is genuinely generative. The training scale and multi-task coverage provide foundation-model-like breadth and transferability.","evidence_snippet":"\"multimodal LLM\"; \"natural-language instructions\"; \"free-text biological knowledge and question-answering data\"; \"more than 5.5 million instruction-following examples spanning over 70 task types\"; \"open-ended biological question answering\"; \"language-guided biological reasoning over expression data\""},{"record_id":"june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000246","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The evidence supports a primary generative foundation model rather than a wrapper: it learns a shared representation for transcriptomic profiles inside the LLM context and is trained across many task types. The paper emphasizes broad biological reasoning and QA, not only a single downstream predictor.","evidence_snippet":"\"represents each transcriptomic profile as a compact continuous representation within the LLM context\"; \"preserves quantitative expression signal while allowing natural-language instructions\"; \"trained ... spanning over 70 task types\"; \"open-ended biological question answering\"; \"language-guided, multi-sample reasoning over real expression profiles\"; \"outperforming both omics-specialized models and general LLMs\"; \"continuous vector\"; \"LLM token-embedding space\"; \"multiple profiles can be interleaved in one prompt\""}]}
